I'm starting to play Knights now, and I am slightly worried that so
many low-level Knights have died when they try to mount their steed,
but instead slip off and take lethal damage.  So I was wondering what
is the exact damage range a character can take when the #ride command
fails.

I did find this piece of code in steed.c:
320.  	    You("slip while trying to get on %s.", mon_nam(mtmp));
321.
322.  	    Sprintf(buf, "slipped while mounting %s",
323.  		    /* "a saddled mumak" or "a saddled pony called Dobbin" */
324.  		    x_monnam(mtmp, ARTICLE_A, (char *)0,
325.  			SUPPRESS_IT|SUPPRESS_INVISIBLE|SUPPRESS_HALLUCINATION,
326.  			     TRUE));
327.  	    losehp(rn1(5,10), buf, NO_KILLER_PREFIX);
328.  	    return (FALSE);

And I did find this piece of code in hack.h:
291.  #define rn1(x,y)	(rn2(x)+(y))

And I did find this piece of code in Rnd.c:
22.   rn2(x)		/* 0 <= rn2(x) < x */


When I combine this all together, I get the following:
1) rn1(5,10)
2) rn2(5)+(10)
3) (random number between 0 and 4) + 10
4) random number between 10 and 14

So is it safe to say that if I have at least 15 HP, that I can't die
from slipping of my steed when the #ride command fails?


